  "$comment": "Hint book for scripts/model_router.py: each job names a provider and a model family (a pattern over ids, with a version group) plus the capabilities it needs (for Google, the generation methods it calls), never a model id. The router picks the newest active, generally available model in that family, at least 14 days old, from the provider's live list. default_alias names the scripts/model_registry.json alias used when the list cannot be read. 'deprecations' records what an agent read from the provider's deprecations page, because Google's model list reports no lifecycle and no release date; re-read it within 30 days and update read_on. Every rule and record carries the page it was read from and the date.",
